From a2d3366bdc58a99f5d81313d71d8a384c402ecda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Try Omarchy Release <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:28:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Ship Wau OS in the Omarchy guest

The guest carries Omarchy as its runtime. Wau OS belongs to that runtime, so
two things have to reach the image: the Wau OS package, and the first-run
step that sets Wau OS up on a new account.

The package is installed from a verified archive after the locked transaction,
never resolved from a live repository, and its compositor dependencies join
the transaction itself. The first-run step is an overlay on the pinned
Omarchy runtime: every file it replaces carries the digest of the upstream
file it was reviewed against.
